From: ReadyNAS NG <readynasng@build>
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] crypto: sparc32: fast AES-CMAC for sparc v7

SMB 3 signing (ksmbd, ksmbd_sign_smb3_pdu) is cmac(aes), which resolved
to the cmac template over aes-generic (priority 100; aes-fixed-time is
not built). Per 16-byte block that path does crypto_xor() on the state
in memory, crypto_cipher_encrypt_one() and the cipher through a pointer
(two register windows), little-endian byte loads and stores of the block,
and an encryption fully unrolled for 10/12/14 rounds (about 4 KiB of code
for AES-128) that walks 8 KiB of tables: crypto_ft_tab for nine rounds,
crypto_fl_tab for the last. On the Padre, whose caches are a few KiB,
signing costs about 0.35 s of CPU per MiB, three times an unsigned
transfer.

cmac-aes-sparc32 (priority 200) registers cmac(aes) as one shash whose
update runs the whole CBC-MAC chain in one function:

- state in registers from the first block to the last, block loaded and
  xored straight into it, no call per block;
- encryption only, two rounds per loop iteration (about 1.2 KiB of code);
- each table index built in two instructions (srl/sll, and 0x3fc: the
  byte already scaled by 4), then one ld: about 70 instructions a round,
  no spill (gcc -mcpu=v7 output checked);
- the last round reads S[x] as byte 1 of crypto_ft_tab[0][x] (the same in
  either byte order), so 4 KiB of tables in all instead of 8;
- round keys from aes_expandkey(), tables from aes-generic: no new table,
  no new key schedule. K1/K2 and the final block as crypto/cmac.c
  (Jussi Kivilinna), block-only buffering left to the shash core.

About 780 instructions per AES-128 block against about 1 010 (encrypt,
xor, calls), with half the D-cache footprint and a third of the hot code.
Estimated 1.4 to 1.8 times the CMAC throughput, i.e. signed SMB
transfers from about 2.2 to 2.5-3 MiB/s, the rest being the unsigned
path; to be confirmed on the NAS with the user-space benchmark built
from this same file (cmacbench).

Not constant time, like aes-generic which it replaces for this use: the
table addresses depend on key and data. The constant-time choices are
slower here: aes-fixed-time (lib/crypto/aes.c, S-box only, MixColumns
computed) takes more instructions per round, and bitsliced or fixsliced
AES needs several blocks in parallel where CBC-MAC has one. ksmbd only offers AES-CMAC and HMAC-SHA256
(no AES-GMAC; GHASH without a multiplier would be slower anyway), and
HMAC-SHA256 is not cheaper on this CPU.

Checked: NIST SP 800-38B / RFC 4493 vectors (AES-128 and AES-256) and
3000 random messages (128/192/256-bit keys, split in two kvecs, any
alignment) against cmac(aes-generic), under qemu-sparc with mul/div
disabled. With CONFIG_CRYPTO_SELFTESTS the crypto manager runs the
cmac(aes) vectors on registration (and with _FULL compares against
cmac(aes-generic) on random inputs).
---
 arch/sparc/crypto/Kconfig            |  18 ++-
 arch/sparc/crypto/Makefile           |   1 +
 arch/sparc/crypto/cmac-aes-sparc32.c | 225 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 243 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/crypto/Kconfig b/arch/sparc/crypto/Kconfig
index f755da97953462276a6411c0cf749a484196c334..da1f4f89b1ec3412181f5bbf4f5d657e7c84a348 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/crypto/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/sparc/crypto/Kconfig
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 
-menu "Accelerated Cryptographic Algorithms for CPU (sparc64)"
+menu "Accelerated Cryptographic Algorithms for CPU (sparc)"
 
 config CRYPTO_DES_SPARC64
 	tristate "Ciphers: DES and Triple DES EDE, modes: ECB/CBC"
@@ -37,4 +37,20 @@ config CRYPTO_CAMELLIA_SPARC64
 
 	  Architecture: sparc64
 
+config CRYPTO_CMAC_AES_SPARC32
+	tristate "Hash functions: AES-CMAC (sparc32 v7)"
+	depends on SPARC32
+	select CRYPTO_AES
+	select CRYPTO_LIB_AES
+	select CRYPTO_HASH
+	help
+	  AES-CMAC (NIST SP 800-38B, RFC 4493) as one function per update:
+	  CBC-MAC state in registers, encryption only, 4 KiB of tables
+	  (crypto_ft_tab).  For CPUs with small caches and slow calls, such
+	  as the Infrant Padre: SMB 3 signing in ksmbd is cmac(aes).
+
+	  Table-based, like aes-generic: not constant time.
+
+	  Architecture: sparc32
+
 endmenu
diff --git a/arch/sparc/crypto/Makefile b/arch/sparc/crypto/Makefile
index 7b4796842ddd7c52b66e6d196142e684b023a5bd..f8cbd28efc868ac09e4d3619b5a80ea64896c262 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/crypto/Makefile
